WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.550
In the eighth century BC,
the kings of Urartu

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.119
ruled the highlands around Lake Van
from their rock citadel at Tushpa.

3
00:00:10.159 --> 00:00:12.452
They called their land Biainili.

4
00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:16.022
Under Argishti I, son of Menua,

5
00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:18.698
the kingdom stood
near the height of its power.

6
00:00:18.738 --> 00:00:21.187
He pushed north of the Araxes.

7
00:00:21.547 --> 00:00:26.237
There, in 782 BC
by the date most often given,

8
00:00:26.277 --> 00:00:29.497
he raised a new fortress
on the hill of Arin Berd,

9
00:00:29.537 --> 00:00:31.960
and named it Erebuni.

10
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.750
His founding inscription,
cut in cuneiform,

11
00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.435
was found on the hill in 1950.

12
00:00:38.795 --> 00:00:41.225
Argishti also fought Assyria,

13
00:00:41.265 --> 00:00:44.454
but those wars were fought
far from Erebuni.

14
00:00:44.494 --> 00:00:46.924
No siege of it is recorded:

15
00:00:46.964 --> 00:00:51.104
the march you are about to face
is an invention of the game.

16
00:00:51.464 --> 00:00:54.210
Yet the name lives on in Yerevan.

17
00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.693
Defend the young city.

